# Copy to $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/environment.d/podrc.conf (make
# install-session-env does this automatically if the destination doesn't
# already exist) to set XDG_CONFIG_HOME session-wide, read by
# systemd --user's environment.d generator (environment.d(5)) at session
# start -- not just interactive shells, but GUI apps and every
# systemd --user service in the session. Takes effect on next login (or
# `systemctl --user daemon-reexec`).
#
# Commented out by default: ~/.config is already the fallback this repo's
# own hack/ scripts and installed units use when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset,
# so there's nothing to do unless you want it somewhere else. %h is the
# systemd specifier for the invoking user's home directory (same one used
# throughout this repo's quadlet units), expanded by systemd itself, not
# a shell.

#XDG_CONFIG_HOME=%h/.config
